@startuml events_dispatch
title Domain events: publication, routing and live/offline delivery
autonumber
participant "CLI document client" as Client
box "hermes-document-service" #E0F4E0
participant "API + middleware" as API
participant "internal/app" as App
participant "internal/domain" as Domain
participant "internal/postgres" as Repo
participant "Auth + Redis SessionStore" as Sessions
participant "internal/kafka\nDomainEventPublisher" as Publisher
end box
database "Document PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "notification-service\nConsumer / routing" as HNS
participant "Active WebSocket connections\nAll HNS instances" as Connections
database "Notification PostgreSQL\nPending offline messages" as Inbox

== Domain mutation ==
Client -> API : Protected command(session, expected_version)
ref over API, Sessions : Validate session through Auth + Redis (auth.puml)
API -> App : Use case(authenticated identity, validated request)
App -> Repo : WithinTransaction: load current domain state
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; read/lock current state
App -> Domain : Check current permissions, invariants and version
alt Rejected / persistence failure
  Repo -> DB : ROLLBACK
  App --> API : Error; no committed change facts
  API --> Client : Error
else No actual change
  Repo -> DB : COMMIT without mutation
  App --> API : Unchanged result; no change event
  API --> Client : Result
else Valid change
  App -> Repo : Persist domain changes
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE / INSERT / DELETE
  opt OPEN: outbox/CDC selected as reliable publication mechanism
    App -> Repo : Persist event intent atomically with domain changes
    Repo -> DB : Transactional outbox record / selected CDC source
  end
  Repo -> DB : COMMIT
  DB --> Repo : Confirmed / unknown outcome
  Repo --> App : Transaction result
  App --> API : Success only after confirmed domain commit / outcome unknown
  API --> Client : Result; never claim rollback from a lost response
end
note over App, DB
  Only facts from committed changes may be published; no facts for reads/errors/no-op.
  A timeout during COMMIT can leave an unknown outcome.
  Event intent above is conditional, not a selected outbox implementation.
end note

== Publish committed domain facts ==
opt Confirmed committed change with domain facts
alt OPEN option: direct publication after commit
  App -> Publisher : Publish(committed facts) through owned interface
  Publisher -> Kafka : DomainEvent(event_id, type, schema_version, IDs, versions, payload)
  Kafka --> Publisher : Broker ack / timeout / failure
  Publisher --> App : Publication outcome
  note over App, Kafka
    Commit-to-publish crash window can lose an event.
    Success/error response semantics and retry policy remain OPEN (ADR-002).
    Kafka failure cannot roll back an already committed PostgreSQL mutation.
  end note
else OPEN option: outbox/CDC
  ref over Repo, Kafka
    Selected publisher/relay reads committed intent and publishes asynchronously.
    Claiming, retries, acknowledgement and retention require a separate protocol.
    Broker acceptance followed by a crash may cause duplicate delivery.
  end ref
end
note over Publisher, Kafka
  Kafka channel is accepted; reliability, ordering and replay are OPEN.
  Preserve event_id across retries; never include tokens, credentials,
  private emails or document bodies in event payloads.
end note
end

== Consume, select policy and recipients ==
Kafka -> HNS : Domain event
HNS -> HNS : Validate schema; select live signal / personal-notice policy
ref over HNS
  OPEN: resolve current recipients and authorization data.
  Internal HDS API / projection / Redis rights are alternatives, not accepted contracts.
  Do not query document PostgreSQL directly or use session as workspace permission.
end ref
HNS -> HNS : Apply user settings; exclude ineligible/deleted recipients;\nsuppress actor except ProfileChanged; merge recipient reasons
note over HNS
  Unsupported schema, poison records, retries and replay require explicit policy.
  Event may produce a live refresh, a personal notice, both or neither.
  Invitations remain discoverable through HDS even if category is disabled.
end note

== Route to each eligible recipient ==
loop Each recipient selected by policy
  HNS -> HNS : Resolve active connections across HNS instances (coordination OPEN)
  alt Recipient has active connections
    HNS -> Connections : Fan out to ALL active sessions/connections of recipient
    Connections -> Client : WebSocket message
    note over HNS, Client
      A socket write is not a client receipt or read acknowledgement.
      Live delivery does not require a durable inbox write first.
    end note
  else No active connection
    HNS -> Inbox : Persist recipient's pending message
    Inbox --> HNS : Stored / failed / outcome unknown
    note over HNS, Inbox
      Offline storage follows arch/notes.txt; message classes and exact policy OPEN.
      Concurrent connect/disconnect between lookup and send requires a protocol.
      Failure after partial fan-out, retries and duplicate suppression remain OPEN.
    end note
  end
end
HNS -> Kafka : Commit offset only under agreed processing/delivery policy (OPEN)
note over Kafka, Inbox
  No promise of exactly-once delivery or permanent history.
  Consumer restart and repeated events must be covered by selected dedup/replay rules.
  PostgreSQL receipts/unique keys are options, not established live delivery semantics.
  Exclusion during fan-out must not leak content after access revocation;
  routing freshness and revocation bounds remain OPEN.
end note
@enduml
